{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "def check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    This function utilizes a helper to reverse the input number.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _get_reverse(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the reverse of a given non-negative integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        reversed_num = 0\n        original_num = num\n        while original_num > 0:\n            digit = original_num % 10\n            reversed_num = reversed_num * 10 + digit\n            original_num //= 10\n        return reversed_num\n\n    reversed_number = _get_reverse(number)\n    return number == (2 * reversed_number) - 1"}
