{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number.\n    Uses dynamic programming for Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    stirling = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling[i][j] = stirling[i - 1][j - 1] + j * stirling[i - 1][j]\n\n    bell = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell += stirling[n][k]\n\n    return bell"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "def is_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a sublist is contiguously present within a main list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True  # An empty list is always a sublist.\n    if m > n:\n        return False  # A sublist cannot be longer than the main list.\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i + m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False"}
