{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "import math\ndef _calculate_sum_of_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given positive integer n.\n    A proper divisor of n is a positive divisor of n, other than n itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    sum_divs = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for n > 1\n    # Iterate from 2 up to sqrt(n)\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            sum_divs += i\n            if i * i != n:  # Avoid double counting for perfect squares\n                sum_divs += n // i\n    return sum_divs\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sums all amicable numbers within the range from 1 up to the specified limit.\n    An amicable pair (a, b) consists of two distinct positive integers such that\n    the sum of proper divisors of a equals b and the sum of proper divisors of b equals a.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    processed_numbers = set()\n\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if i in processed_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        d_i = _calculate_sum_of_proper_divisors(i)\n        j = d_i\n\n        # Check conditions for an amicable pair\n        if i != j and j > 0 and j <= limit:\n            d_j = _calculate_sum_of_proper_divisors(j)\n            if d_j == i:\n                # Found an amicable pair (i, j)\n                total_sum += i\n                total_sum += j\n                processed_numbers.add(i)\n                processed_numbers.add(j)\n    return total_sum"}
