{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring.\n    This is achieved by transforming '0's to 1 and '1's to -1, then applying Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    transformed_array = []\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_array.append(1)\n        elif char == '1':\n            transformed_array.append(-1)\n\n    max_so_far = 0  # Represents the maximum difference found so far\n    current_max = 0 # Represents the maximum difference ending at the current position\n\n    for num in transformed_array:\n        current_max += num\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum_common_divisors(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two given numbers.\n    It first finds the greatest common divisor (GCD) and then sums all divisors of the GCD.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _gcd(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the greatest common divisor of two positive integers using the Euclidean algorithm.\"\"\"\n        while b:\n            a, b = b, a % b\n        return a\n\n    common_gcd = _gcd(num1, num2)\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, common_gcd + 1):\n        if common_gcd % i == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in a given list.\n    Raises ValueError if input_list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    counts = {}\n    for item in input_list:\n        counts[item] = counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    max_item = None\n    max_freq = -1\n\n    for item, freq in counts.items():\n        if freq > max_freq:\n            max_freq = freq\n            max_item = item\n\n    return max_item"}
