{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def _create_canonical_tuple(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms an input tuple into its canonical (sorted) representation.\n    This helper function sorts the elements within the tuple and returns a new tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(input_tuple))\ndef check_occurences(tuple_list: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the occurrence count for canonical representations of tuples in a list.\n    Tuples with the same elements but different order are treated as identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrence_map = {}\n    for input_tuple in tuple_list:\n        canonical_tuple = _create_canonical_tuple(input_tuple)\n        occurrence_map[canonical_tuple] = occurrence_map.get(canonical_tuple, 0) + 1\n    return occurrence_map"}
