{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0-indexed from the right) of the given number to 1.\n    Returns the modified integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Construct a mask with all even bits set to 1, covering up to 64 bits for practical range.\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(0, 64, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply bitwise OR to set all even-positioned bits to 1, leaving odd bits unchanged.\n    return number | mask"}
