{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    increasing_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                increasing_sums[i] = max(increasing_sums[i], increasing_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    decreasing_sums = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                decreasing_sums[i] = max(decreasing_sums[i], decreasing_sums[j] + arr[i])\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = increasing_sums[i] + decreasing_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\ndef convert(complex_number: complex) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a complex number to its polar coordinates (magnitude and angle).\n    The angle is returned in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    real = complex_number.real\n    imaginary = complex_number.imag\n    \n    magnitude = math.sqrt(real**2 + imaginary**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(imaginary, real)\n    \n    return (magnitude, angle)"}
