{"task_id": "Mbpp/273", "solution": "def substract_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts elements of the second tuple from the first tuple element-wise.\n    Validates input types, tuple lengths, and element types.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for elem1, elem2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if not isinstance(elem1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(elem2, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements within the tuples must be numeric (int or float).\")\n        result.append(elem1 - elem2)\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
