{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n\n    Args:\n        arr: A list of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing the two integers that yield the highest product.\n        Returns (0, 0) if the array has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return (0, 0)\n\n    arr.sort()\n\n    # The highest product will either be from the two largest numbers\n    # or from the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    prod1 = arr[0] * arr[1]\n    prod2 = arr[-1] * arr[-2]\n\n    if prod1 > prod2:\n        return (arr[0], arr[1])\n    else:\n        return (arr[-2], arr[-1])"}
