{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "def and_tuples(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an element-wise bitwise AND operation on two input tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if tuples have different lengths, or TypeError if elements are not integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        val1 = tuple1[i]\n        val2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(val1, int) or not isinstance(val2, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Tuple elements must be integers\")\n\n        result.append(val1 & val2)\n\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    Modifies the input list in-place and returns it.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return arr"}
