{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "def Find_Min(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a given list of lists.\n    If multiple sublists have the same minimum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        # As per design, raise ValueError for empty input list.\n        # This aligns with the \"Error Handling\" section in \"System Interfaces\".\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        # As per design, check if elements are lists.\n        # This aligns with the \"Input Validation\" in \"System Implementation\".\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in the input list must be lists.\")\n\n        current_length = len(sublist)\n        if current_length < min_length:\n            min_length = current_length\n            min_sublist = sublist\n            \n    return min_sublist"}
