{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[float | int], list2: list[float | int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size. This uses a merge-like approach to find the two middle elements.\"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2\n    m1 = -1.0  # Stores the (N/2)-th element\n    m2 = -1.0  # Stores the (N/2 + 1)-th element\n\n    # Iterate size + 1 times to find the two middle elements\n    # For a combined list of 2*size elements, the median is (elements at index size-1 + element at index size) / 2\n    # We loop size+1 times to ensure we capture both m1 (at index size-1) and m2 (at index size)\n    for _ in range(size + 1):\n        m1 = m2  # m1 becomes the element found in the previous iteration\n\n        if i < size and j < size:\n            if list1[i] < list2[j]:\n                m2 = float(list1[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                m2 = float(list2[j])\n                j += 1\n        elif i < size:  # list2 is exhausted\n            m2 = float(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:  # list1 is exhausted (j < size must be true)\n            m2 = float(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
