{"task_id": "Mbpp/722", "solution": "class Student:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates student data and provides methods to check if criteria are met.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, height: float, weight: float):\n        self.name = name\n        self.height = height\n        self.weight = weight\n\n    def meets_height_criteria(self, minimal_height: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the student's height meets the minimal height criterion.\"\"\"\n        return self.height >= minimal_height\n\n    def meets_weight_criteria(self, minimal_weight: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the student's weight meets the minimal weight criterion.\"\"\"\n        return self.weight >= minimal_weight\nclass Criteria:\n    \"\"\"Stores the minimal height and minimal weight thresholds for filtering.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, minimal_height: float, minimal_weight: float):\n        self.minimal_height = minimal_height\n        self.minimal_weight = minimal_weight\ndef filter_data(student_data: dict[str, tuple[float, float]], minimal_height: float, minimal_weight: float) -> dict[str, tuple[float, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Filters a dictionary of students based on provided minimal height and weight criteria.\"\"\"\n    filtered_students_dict = {}\n    criteria = Criteria(minimal_height, minimal_weight)\n\n    for name, (height, weight) in student_data.items():\n        student = Student(name, height, weight)\n        if student.meets_height_criteria(criteria.minimal_height) and \\\n           student.meets_weight_criteria(criteria.minimal_weight):\n            filtered_students_dict[name] = (height, weight)\n            \n    return filtered_students_dict"}
