{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last (highest) position of a given element in a sorted array using a modified binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further occurrences to the right\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/796", "solution": "from typing import Dict, Union\ndef return_sum(input_dict: Dict[str, Union[int, float, str, bool, None]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all numeric values in the given dictionary.\n    Non-numeric values are ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_dict, dict):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a dictionary.\")\n\n    total_sum: Union[int, float] = 0\n    for value in input_dict.values():\n        if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n            total_sum += value\n    return total_sum"}
