{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(n: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit unsigned integer 'n' to the left by 'd' positions.\n    Bits shifted out from the MSB are re-inserted at the LSB.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_LENGTH = 32\n    # Ensure n is treated as a 32-bit unsigned integer by masking.\n    n_32bit = n & ((1 << BIT_LENGTH) - 1)\n\n    # Calculate the effective rotation amount modulo BIT_LENGTH.\n    effective_d = d % BIT_LENGTH\n\n    if effective_d == 0:\n        return n_32bit\n\n    # Perform the left shift and wrap-around operation.\n    part1 = (n_32bit << effective_d)\n    part2 = (n_32bit >> (BIT_LENGTH - effective_d))\n\n    # Combine the two parts and ensure the final result is within 32 bits.\n    result = (part1 | part2) & ((1 << BIT_LENGTH) - 1)\n\n    return result"}
